<cell id="cell-5"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Step 3: Fetch corpus.jsonl + Axolotl YAML from secret gists

Drive-free, fully autonomous — no file picker. STRONGARM + Gremlin merged corpus is hosted as a secret gist (URL-only, not publicly searchable) and SHA-256 verified after fetch.

**Replace the two placeholder gist URLs and `EXPECTED_CORPUS_SHA` below with the values from receipt #032 before running.** The notebook will refuse to proceed on SHA mismatch.</cell id="cell-5">
<cell id="cell-6">import os, json, urllib.request, hashlib

# === REPLACE THESE THREE VALUES (from receipt #032 — AE Misfit corpus assignment) ===
CORPUS_URL = 'https://gist.githubusercontent.com/AtomEons/REPLACE_WITH_AE_MISFIT_CORPUS_GIST_ID/raw/corpus.jsonl'
YAML_URL = 'https://gist.githubusercontent.com/AtomEons/REPLACE_WITH_AE_MISFIT_YAML_GIST_ID/raw/ae-misfit-v0.yaml'
EXPECTED_CORPUS_SHA = 'REPLACE_WITH_SHA256_FROM_RECEIPT_032'
# ====================================================================================

corpus_path = f'{WORK_DIR}/corpus.jsonl'
config_path = f'{WORK_DIR}/ae-misfit-v0.yaml'

def fetch(url, dest):
    print(f'Fetching {url}')
    with urllib.request.urlopen(url) as r, open(dest, 'wb') as f:
        f.write(r.read())
    print(f'  -> {dest} ({os.path.getsize(dest)} bytes)')

fetch(CORPUS_URL, corpus_path)
fetch(YAML_URL, config_path)

h = hashlib.sha256()
with open(corpus_path, 'rb') as f:
    for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1 << 20), b''):
        h.update(chunk)
actual_sha = h.hexdigest()
print(f'\nCorpus SHA-256: {actual_sha}')
print(f'Expected:       {EXPECTED_CORPUS_SHA}')
assert actual_sha == EXPECTED_CORPUS_SHA, 'SHA mismatch — corpus corrupted in transit or wrong gist URL!'
print('SHA verified.')

with open(corpus_path) as f:
    pairs = [json.loads(l) for l in f if l.strip()]
print(f'\nCorpus: {len(pairs)} STRONGARM+Gremlin instruction pairs')
print(f'First pair instruction: {pairs[0]["instruction"][:120]}...')
print(f'First pair output    : {pairs[0]["output"][:120]}...')</cell id="cell-6">
